## asks how the levels differ before saying anything about herself, then which one she should pick

Lead: what's the difference between group and full? and does self paced get the recordings?

Sonia: The difference is how much of me you get. Both have the 16 modules, the live group sessions twice a week with recordings, and the private community.

Full is me by your side every step of the way: up to 2 private 20 minute sessions with me a month, unlimited texting in between, a personalized meal plan and my daily review of the fertility tracker information you send me.

Self paced is the modules and resources only, so no recordings, no community and no coaching.

Lead: so on group could i still get a meal plan made for me?

Sonia: No, the personalized meal plan is part of Full. On Group you'd have the Eat Well module with hundreds of recipes, and the live sessions to bring your questions to.

Lead: and on full can i actually message you whenever?

Sonia: Yes, texting isn't limited to your session times. You can send me updates and questions as they come up, and I'll get back to you, just not instantly at every hour.

Lead: ok. which one would you put me on?

Sonia: That depends on your goals and how much support you want, and it's exactly what my team works out with you on the free call.

Tell me a little about where you are with trying and I'll tell you what I'd be thinking about for you.
